       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. That is 5 times the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. A single 4000 mg dose is also far above the usual maximum of 800 mg. At this level the risks include serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO QID** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO TID** (2,400 mg/day), a common maximum-intensity regimen\n- **600 mg PO QID** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg really was intended, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
