       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single 4000 mg dose of ibuprofen, repeated four times a day, is in the toxic range. I don't know of any indication or protocol that calls for it, and the risk of serious harm to the patient is high. Confirming it doesn't change that, and you haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If it's a typo or a misremembered dose,** give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. Examples are 400 mg QID, 600 mg QID, or 800 mg TID.\n- **If there's a specific reason for this dose,** discuss it with your attending and a clinical pharmacist. If they approve it, the order can go through whatever override or verification process your hospital uses.\n- **If the aim is stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory effect,** I can enter a standard ibuprofen regimen. Your team could also consider adjuncts such as acetaminophen, or a different agent.\n\nI can enter any of the first or third options as soon as you tell me which one."
